{"title":"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Hungary</i>)\nSolve the system of equations:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e39dc8af2ea89645c3f0fe46ad0b62b1dd7570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} \\quad x + y + z \\!\\!\\! &amp;= a \\; \\, \\\\ x^2 +y^2+z^2 \\!\\!\\! &amp;=b^2 \\\\ \\qquad \\qquad xy \\!\\!\\!  &amp;= z^2 \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"138\" height=\"54\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are constants.  Give the conditions that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must satisfy so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> (the solutions of the system) are distinct positive numbers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85e26a852d00c4407f5aca002187cd71e3f7cc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = (x+y)^2 - 2xy = (x+y)^2 - 2z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"331\" height=\"19\" />, so the first two equations become\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/363fa28866c8007078aef5ef00f6cd5d4c3aa9ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} \\quad (x + y) + z \\!\\!\\! &amp;= a \\; \\; (*) \\\\ (x+y)^2 - z^2 \\!\\!\\! &amp;=b^2 (**) \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"177\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab7b88f8c9b9bc6263833c10699527496735d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y)^2 - z^2 = \\Big[ (x+y)+z \\Big]\\Big[ (x+y)-z\\Big]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"332\" height=\"32\" />, so if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> equals 0, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must also equal 0.  We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/4570f2839237362b8f524c6071bb4da3e45328d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = -z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a12cc8b1b81ad3b0d171a928fc12b70100d122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = (x+y)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"19\" />.  This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/92353a1676fd30fac2556a3154f5e567f5b4b5d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + xy + y^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />.  Mutiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40d4d32572cbcecb17e77eaac1354e9b3ffb757e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a2e932daca00a050c6dbde400550e74fda63178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - y^3 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />.  Since we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> to be real, this implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e33fa7c7b2ce1a18e6e0a6d3ef6c08bd1958722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />.  But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/32859989a44bbbfc5fd28d6c1d7dd8ee60dd055a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + x^2 + x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> can only equal 0 when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> (which, in this case, implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f009298d1e620da29263ff83f52d5d00e1fb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,z = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />).  Hence there are no positive solutions when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a8181c9d9b8253bd721b620aaabc5b01f4af96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />, we divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add9aecc4400c0721e215cecc4c2be5c4b18313e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(**)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> to obtain the system of equations\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb777e7d382c1918b3b1bdf81f9463ffb667088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} (x+y)+z &amp;= a \\; \\quad \\\\ (x+y)-z &amp;= b^2/a \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"157\" height=\"38\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which clearly has solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd7ce9339ab49ff41fab6cd31bba070053ca83a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa56001406e53caa4b107621cbac078481513b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\frac{a^2 - b^2}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"39\" />.  In order for these both to be positive, we must have positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a02724a39249b7805087eb9ff41263fff1cf0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />.  Now, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd7ce9339ab49ff41fab6cd31bba070053ca83a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"39\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d648a785c2971a231169deb13053e34ee97c65d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = \\left(\\frac{a^2 - b^2}{2a}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"135\" height=\"47\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> are the roots of the quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e9948e218e2838cf387afee34c47a38cba404571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2a}m + \\left(\\frac{a^2 - b^2}{2a}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"233\" height=\"47\" />.  The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant\" title=\"Discriminant\">discriminant</a> for this equation is\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/9474cc5ed5d48c449bd42e11b778da6a81793a5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2a}\\right)^2 - \\left(2\\frac{a^2 -b^2}{2a}\\right)^2 = \\frac{ (3a^2 - b^2)(3b^2 - a^2) }{4a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"398\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>If the expressions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b25a5d23a22f2b7e1177fd682740d1dccd0c281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3a^2 - b^2), (3b^2 - a^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" /> were simultaneously negative, then their sum, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2add6a7a70b7cd8c3c8184628d7f3c890395fac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a^2 + b^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />, would also be negative, which cannot be.  Therefore our quadratic's discriminant is positive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/0/b60edc1110e409809b0bdbfd803da13d0007d87e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c006e620b0f8332f5a6751b57d5a7ef1faf79b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b^2 &gt; a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />.  But we have already replaced the first inequality with the sharper bound <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a02724a39249b7805087eb9ff41263fff1cf0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />.  It is clear that both roots of the quadratic must be positive if the discriminant is positive (we can see this either from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/cee4abb4ac4b5356519d4f240e71dfb01235f09a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2a}\\right)^2 &gt; \\left(\\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2a}\\right)^2 - \\left(2\\frac{a^2 -b^2}{2a}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"330\" height=\"47\" /> or from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial#Descartes.27_Law_of_Signs\" title=\"Polynomial\"> Descartes' Rule of Signs</a>).  We have now found the solutions to the system, and determined that it has positive solutions if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d7d536442cebb2d8663eabe47c41d53a9d19249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b^2 &gt; a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />.  Q.E.D.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b257bc30eeead5a7b75e290206fb3e6ec5e52732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x+y+z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />. The third equation implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655858b792c42ff896ad69d5afe6b35ba3d17f80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,z,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> is a geometric sequence. Then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fcf3bced8be8cc81ab1301c6eaae94c8e447064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{z}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74bb803e9932af7742291ab82420f57c1f79d2d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=rz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173148bdce1dff2802af5fd307ab26946b419491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5edcc8f911db56af92e4bd91f78fcf7e8b809ecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. Then the first two equations become:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46cef03f9c05e7e8bb4d8a2546f4e80af7786942.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(r+1+\\frac{1}{r}\\right)z=a~~~(1)\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"43\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea3e9522883a65b03e4e6bafac4d40c3fcf233f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(r^2+1+\\frac{1}{r^2}\\right)z^2=b^2~~~(2)\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"43\" />\nTaking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed239efc9ceb8a2b73a10abd7b90fda7ca55733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2)}{(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"29\" height=\"45\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b762d600896ea82c99d490b90c0c0d11ee4938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />), we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0edf7a06afa8b92ca2b92a137662843db5cc6b59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(r^2+1+\\frac{1}{r^2})z^2}{(r+1+\\frac{1}{r})z}=\\left(r-1+\\frac{1}{r}\\right)z=\\frac{b^2}{a}~~~(3)\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"47\" />\nWe can then take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e9583664f31515950779d166d13961471f57c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)^2-(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be6bfb0a195a4d6f2bc54e48c2f44263a791d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)-(3)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" /> to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f40468a8555426d6ede0de05f7b36f93034a5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(r^2+2r+3+\\frac{2}{r}+\\frac{1}{r^2}\\right)z^2-\\left(r^2+1+\\frac{1}{r^2}\\right)z^2=2z^2\\left(r+1+\\frac{1}{r}\\right)=a^2-b^2~~~(4)\\]\" width=\"615\" height=\"43\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48107a7e2c84b27e4d2c6657daa0acd568e95a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(r^2+1+\\frac{1}{r^2}\\right)z^2-\\left(r^2-2r+3-\\frac{2}{r}+\\frac{1}{r^2}\\right)z^2=2z^2\\left(r-1+\\frac{1}{r}\\right)=b^2-\\frac{b^4}{a^2}=\\frac{b^2}{a^2}(a^2-b^2)~~~(5)\\]\" width=\"725\" height=\"43\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c2b346578548d23b2f7362bb877b5f800605aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=r+\\frac{1}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />. By AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291d1481161e5339e53d6caea42174d1a0d71898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> with equality at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e623703651407c3ee100d9ad4314567a5ec1f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{1}{r}\\implies r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" />, which is impossible. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c877cdefa36f90cdf80f93dadc93cc77d19961a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d42b1119c6f82026e6c57eaf9cfdcc2628372c45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(5)}{(4)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"29\" height=\"45\" /> becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d082b4fcc45efc0dab9e95f4a13a1c9a5e8a7baf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{k-1}{k+1}=\\frac{b^2}{a^2}~(6)\\implies a^2+b^2=(a^2-b^2)k&gt;2(a^2-b^2)\\implies3b^2&gt;a^2\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"41\" />\nFrom the above restrictions on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we see that there must exist some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c877cdefa36f90cdf80f93dadc93cc77d19961a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8597460a07f59450a07e0f94607fcb479cf974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, and hence, some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cffcfc4fb2e7a492660eee9e0787841b6c4aae58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;0\\neq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8597460a07f59450a07e0f94607fcb479cf974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104992efa4deaa9a2dfeeec9b331ad0bf628f80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02ef7389506f1c179cc6b47141004128dffdac3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-b^2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, then there must exist some positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104992efa4deaa9a2dfeeec9b331ad0bf628f80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" />, and consequently since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104992efa4deaa9a2dfeeec9b331ad0bf628f80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8597460a07f59450a07e0f94607fcb479cf974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> are equivalent to the remaining equations, they satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> satisfy the original system, and from the restrictions on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, they are distinct positive reals. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015dfe6deda2858f48e6b9a629e9f87398e4fc06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{a&gt;0\\text{ and }3b^2&gt;a^2&gt;b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"199\" height=\"29\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~rhydon516\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>While we do not have access to the grading rubric, we can infer that it should require checking off the following items.\n</p><p>- Demonstrating that it is necessary and sufficient for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to take on some arbitrary positive value.\n</p><p>- Demonstrating that it is necessary and sufficient that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> falls in the open interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d61977a895476da9528d18da1542b84b8084314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a^2}{3}, a^2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"74\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>- Finding the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> corresponding to the selections for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We can chip away at this problem with standard tactics and delegate the last step to solutions 1 and 2 above.\n</p><p>The first critical observation is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are required to be positive so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is required to be positive.\n</p><p>Secondly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56aa9171eb6cc7973168e29cd40e4cecacaa55f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x+y+z)^2}{3} &gt; \\frac{x^2+y^2+z^2}{3} &gt; \\left[\\frac{x+y+z}{3}\\right]^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"353\" height=\"48\" /> for distinct positive values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809482c43ce4dfb1ac227100ca120782b2147951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^2}{3} &gt; \\frac{b^2}{3} &gt; \\frac{a^2}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"41\" /> which forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> into the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d61977a895476da9528d18da1542b84b8084314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a^2}{3}, a^2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"74\" height=\"45\" /> interval.\n</p><p>The final simplification is to note that any solution has a corresponding solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afabd6715b9c9c2590e6b275e65b1fe220990bef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39; = \\frac{a}{a} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/8/1d8b1a2ee6843e47ec2c890abc904da9da9ceee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39; = \\left|\\frac{b}{a}\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"64\" height=\"45\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19fe58f0229a813c231f94ab0f56de44563ed52e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}, 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"73\" height=\"45\" />, which is an allowed operation since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is non-zero and subsequently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152fd259d0945d940b4f78258a65536908d58538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x&#39;, y&#39;, z&#39;) = \\left(\\frac{x}{a}, \\frac{y}{a}, \\frac{z}{a}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"179\" height=\"35\" /> will satisfy all the required constraints. Likewise any solution with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in the necessary interval can be scaled up or down by any positive factor (with the sign on b optionally flipped since it won't affect anything), proving that all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are attainable and likewise all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in the required range.\n</p><p>Now that the problem is simplified we can utilize the techniques from solutions (1) and (2) to solve the specific case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> falls in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19fe58f0229a813c231f94ab0f56de44563ed52e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}, 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"73\" height=\"45\" /> and we should satisfy all the requirements to get a 7 on this problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will simplify the problem by changing the coordinate system. Consider the orthonormal coordinate system <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcae97afd50afd36ef27d7eeff7e8a693e403e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u,v,w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/3063a0d0d5b6fcf9a8737b46210a39e128611669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hat{e}_u = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(1,1,1), \\hat{e}_v = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(1,-1,0), \\hat{e}_w = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}(1,1,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"429\" height=\"43\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80ba942eb18901d0980267529ebd956dcf6acba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z) = u\\hat{e}_u + v\\hat{e}_v + w\\hat{e}_w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" /> it follows \n\\begin{align}\nx &amp;= \\frac{u}{\\sqrt{3}} + \\frac{v}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{w}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \ny &amp;= \\frac{u}{\\sqrt{3}} - \\frac{v}{\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{w}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\\nz &amp;= \\frac{u}{\\sqrt{3}} - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} w.\n\\end{align}  \nAdding yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f8c30deb12b6a7268d96aacf96132202d5f1ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x+y+z = \\sqrt{3}u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"23\" />. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de1233998c7c03aed5ad55e2eaa0b9dd2217d974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2 + v^2 + w^2 = b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting these values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4da1a8d048588d3b10e472a1baa157a59f2eb58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/17851bd52ef980b022869b1a8d5c7ce69e366e0a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bigg(\\frac{u}{\\sqrt{3}} + \\frac{w}{\\sqrt{6}} \\bigg)^2 - \\frac{v^2}{2} = \\bigg(\\frac{u}{\\sqrt{3}} - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} w\\bigg)^2\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"47\" />\ni.e.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51f28218cc326a67c15356ff46a73fa83cf44984.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\sqrt{2}uw = v^2 + w^2 = b^2 - \\frac{a^2}{3} \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"39\" />\nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/1503d3514202b327855797c60d9c175cf40c70ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2+v^2+w^2 = b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/61576ba708f3c2ea80e013993c1cd6d008775fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}u = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /></b>: \n</p><p>Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d43eae6892d884f8e8f4345b93c83fcf7db3481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7a58270d4285821716c6093a83541f3ea31dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 0$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/84233774bf550c247c8271a5884fbbaa129affcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = v = w = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/1503d3514202b327855797c60d9c175cf40c70ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2+v^2+w^2 = b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. It follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/1322885eabf349cd5173ba9e3a6673a0dbfc1862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p><b>Case</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a8181c9d9b8253bd721b620aaabc5b01f4af96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p>By <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd326f33913b2eac7e8f960815c55cb0a2b8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"65\" height=\"39\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2aa0d67ca10a94a7e9ba9cacf5214e78d04709.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w = \\frac{1}{2a}\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\Big(b^2 - \\frac{a^2}{3}\\Big).\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"43\" />\nSubstituting our values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e2ada02df6af2f9f33c4906294203f3d614cd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v^2 = b^2 - u^2 - w^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5be8140754a517a58e4903a75bd52ca999c22818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v^2 = b^2 - \\frac{a^2}{3} - \\frac{3}{8a^2}\\Big(b^2-\\frac{a^2}{3}\\Big)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"241\" height=\"41\" /> hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12ce613488dd2e7f67fe70073754449897ced36e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v = \\pm \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}a}\\sqrt{(3b^2-a^2)(3a^2-b^2)}.\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"41\" />\nIn order for this to be real we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e784aa6d9c6ecab93820b4c8253b1c637aa2d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a^2 - b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6bc67f1d14a46bf98c10fbe358c1eb3a910570a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3b^2 - a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> to be the same sign or both equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, however a simple inspection shows they can't both be negative. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852ba14ce4affa0dc18577ae35665cb17b8710dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a^2 - b^2, 3b^2-a^2 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" />, in which case substituting our values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcae97afd50afd36ef27d7eeff7e8a693e403e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u,v,w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> into our equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> yields  \n\\begin{align}\nx &amp;= \\frac{a^2+b^2}{4a} \\pm \\frac{1}{4a}\\sqrt{(3b^2-a^2)(3a^2-b^2)} \\\\\ny &amp;= \\frac{a^2+b^2}{4a} \\mp \\frac{1}{4a}\\sqrt{(3b^2-a^2)(3a^2-b^2)} \\\\\nz &amp;= \\frac{a^2-b^2}{2a}\n\\end{align}\nand one can check that these values indeed satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f64c983320a56ce714a225f9a17b22ff1d91c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z = a, x^2+y^2+z^2 = b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"253\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4da1a8d048588d3b10e472a1baa157a59f2eb58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. Now, we already showed if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83ef77f2ff75dd65865fcb790b7e3dfe4518bfe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=z=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />. By the above equations, clearly then for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> to be positive and distinct its necessary that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/6321aff70ccf2e6770e1e128418587064802a9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, 3a^2 - b^2, 3b^2-a^2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />. Assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, by our equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b762d600896ea82c99d490b90c0c0d11ee4938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a02724a39249b7805087eb9ff41263fff1cf0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f03c82ea83898030263310281bc4925d165c9ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, 3b^2 &gt; a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> is necessary for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> to be positive and distinct. \n</p><p>Sufficiency: assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9a99ac93970d954021dd4fed67d24137e2b9a71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0, 3b^2 &gt; a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />. Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b762d600896ea82c99d490b90c0c0d11ee4938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b4a78db8f086f7169b9a0cc443e0b9ee0224ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=z$\" width=\"43\" height=\"8\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4da1a8d048588d3b10e472a1baa157a59f2eb58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636739c8201322993086908b20be3eceb4a7854d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"11\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />. On the other hand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are distinct by the equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9fdd77eaf8f8070816f597afe84472b80cef08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />. Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c0238029e47ae21c551b8ba110870ded10b2a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\neq z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />. This proves distinctness. Now, by the equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0517387c7374eb6cfeae1fb2084bf2b52a7303.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> iff \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/739bd9d8beed54fba07ba25f666a6ea66db831ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^2 + b^2)^2 &gt; (3b^2-a^2)(3a^2-b^2)\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"20\" />\nwhich simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/716b2bb9cfd01944902a3d474edc47f2f2882d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2-b^2)^2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"21\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69ad397210fe86d147054da6630b5ae615365e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9a99ac93970d954021dd4fed67d24137e2b9a71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0, 3b^2 &gt; a^2 &gt; b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" /> is sufficient for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> to be positive and distinct.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_stCjNU0_M4&amp;list=PLa8j0YHOYQQJGzkvK2Sm00zrh0aIQnof8&amp;index=3\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_stCjNU0_M4&amp;list=PLa8j0YHOYQQJGzkvK2Sm00zrh0aIQnof8&amp;index=3</a>\n- AMBRIGGS\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/e5cuvmW0clk\">https://youtu.be/e5cuvmW0clk</a>  [Video Solution by little fermat]\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO\" title=\"1961 IMO\">1961 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017065124\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.061 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 943/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1211/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursio